  "notes": "Composed of {打|だ} (strike, hit) + {鍵|けん} (key). Used for both keyboard typing and piano playing. Common collocations: {打鍵|だけん}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧ (to type/strike keys), {打鍵|だけん}⟦{速度|そくど}→速度：03319_sokudo⟧ (typing speed), {打鍵|だけん}⟦{数|すう}→数：03360_suu⟧ (number of keystrokes), {打鍵|だけん}{音|おん} (keystroke sound). In the mechanical keyboard community, {打鍵|だけん}⟦{感|かん}→〜感：28578_kan⟧ (key feel) and {打鍵|だけん}{音|おん} (key sound) are important qualities. For piano, {打鍵|だけん} refers to the technique of striking the keys, distinct from the more general ⟦{演奏|えんそう}→演奏：01896_ensou⟧ (performance).",
